    <h2 class="article-title">Of Finding Our Way</h2>
    <div class="article-body">{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}
        <p class="article-author-note"><strong>Author's note.</strong> This Article proposes a rallying point for disciples of every Christian tradition. Its picture is not new: Christ the North Star, His Spirit the compass, the scriptures the map. Each part is drawn from scripture that Christians of every tradition receive, and the arrangement adds nothing to the gospel of Jesus Christ. I offer it not as a creed, nor as a correction to any church, but as a place where we may gather and look together toward the One who prayed that all who believe in Him might be one (John 17:20-23). Its only test is the one it sets for itself: does it bring us, together, to Him?</p>{% endif %}
        <p><strong>We hold</strong> <span data-span="s1" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Jesus the Christ as the fixed point by whom every soul may find the way to God</span>. <span data-span="s2" data-article="A09" data-type="direct" data-named="false">He is the way and the life</span>. <span data-span="s3" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">He does not move. He does not change with the seasons, the pressures of an age, or the shifting claims of men</span>. <span data-span="s4" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">What He taught is what He taught. What He was is what He was.</span> <span data-span="s5" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="true">He stands as the unchanging North Star above every traveler's path</span>.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s6" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}Trusting Him as our Guide is more important than understanding Him{% else %}Trusting Him is more important than understanding Him{% endif %}</span>. <span data-span="s7" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}Personal relationship with the Divine takes precedence over accuracy of doctrine{% else %}One's relationship with the Divine takes precedence over the accuracy of their doctrine{% endif %}</span>. <span data-span="s8" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}Correct tenets and sound understanding are desirable, but faithfully following Christ is better{% else %}Correct doctrines and personal knowledge are good, but faith in Him is better{% endif %}</span>. <span data-span="s9" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">Our hope is that, as we submit to Him, God will make our paths straight</span>.</p>
        <p>We also hold that <span data-span="s10" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="true">the Spirit of God is given to each honest conscience as a compass within — a witness that responds to divine reality, drawing us toward what is true and warning us away from what would destroy us</span>. But <span data-span="s11" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the compass in our own hearts is housed in mortal flesh, and mortal flesh carries its own magnetism — our wounds, our fears, our desires, the pull of those we love and of those we resent</span>. So <span data-span="s12" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the compass of the Spirit in us must be calibrated always to the North Star of Christ Himself</span>. <span data-span="s13" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">When the inward whisper points us away from what Christ taught and what Christ was, we know the compass has been disturbed, and we return our sighting to Him</span>.{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %} <span data-span="s29" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">We submit ourselves to God and resist the devil, standing steadfast in the faith and putting on the whole armor of God</span>.{% endif %}</p>{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}
        <p><span data-span="s23" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">To His disciples, Christ promised another Comforter, the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of truth, whom the Father would send in His name to abide with them</span>. <span data-span="s24" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">By His Spirit, God is present with His people, and there is no place beyond His presence</span>. <span data-span="s25" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">The Spirit teaches us and brings to our remembrance all that Christ has said</span>. <span data-span="s26" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">He testifies of Christ, and no one can say that Jesus is Lord but by the Holy Spirit</span>. <span data-span="s27" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">Through the Spirit, God sanctifies His people</span>, and <span data-span="s28" data-article="A09" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">He gives diverse gifts to believers, dividing to each as He wills, for the good of all</span>.</p>{% endif %}
        <p>We further hold that <span data-span="s14" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="true">the scriptures are given as the sure map — the testimony of those who have traveled before us, marking the way and pointing always to the same North Star</span>. <span data-span="s15" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">They experienced their own wrestles with God</span>, and <span data-span="s16" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">through them the Spirit spoke truth that still lights the way when the wilderness grows dark</span>. <span data-span="s17" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Without the map, the compass alone cannot tell us which pathways we have entered or which perils lie ahead</span>.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s18" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Each time we find ourselves lost or uncertain, we have the navigational tools to reorient and find our way again</span>. We hold that <span data-span="s19" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the disciple's walk does not require the approval of any person, tradition, or institution beyond the approval of Christ Himself, who is the only righteous and eternal Judge of human souls</span>.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s20" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We do not walk by the inward whisper alone. We do not walk by written word alone. We walk by Christ, who is the living reference, and by His Spirit, who leads us toward Him and never away</span>. <span data-span="s21" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">The Father who knows our hearts will guide every soul who comes to Him in sincerity</span>, and <span data-span="s22" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the Son who bids us follow has never led any honest disciple astray</span>.</p>{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}
        <p><span data-span="s30" data-article="A09" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Whatever first turned you toward Christ, we rejoice that you seek Him. We may differ on how the map is rightly read, and on which way leads most surely to Him, but let none of us fail to come unto Jesus of Nazareth. Should any instrument we carry, even this one, turn us from Christ or teach us contempt for a fellow traveler, we have surely lost our bearing, and must take our sighting of Him anew.</span></p>{% endif %}
        <div class="article-rjw">
            <p class="rjw-prompt">{% if aoidSecondEdition.on %}When you feel spiritually lost, which do you reach for first — scripture or the Spirit's witness — and do you let it lead you back to Christ, the fixed reference? Which do you tend to neglect?{% else %}When you feel spiritually lost, which do you reach for first — scripture, the Spirit's witness, or Christ as the fixed reference? Which do you tend to neglect?{% endif %}</p>
            <textarea class="rjw-textarea" data-rjw-key="rjw-A09" placeholder="Your reflection (optional)" rows="3" aria-label="Reflect on Of Finding Our Way"></textarea>
        </div>
    </div>